[[:db/retract 17592186113923 :answer-field/choices 17592186113924] [:db/retract 17592186113923 :answer-field/choices 17592186113925] [:db/retract 17592186113923 :answer-field/choices 17592186113926] [:db/retract 17592186113923 :answer-field/choices 17592186113927] [:db/retract 17592186113923 :answer-field/choices 17592186113928] {:db/id 17592186115242 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-db005b4e-86cd-5194-b2fd-10ca4ee59c03"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-db005b4e-86cd-5194-b2fd-10ca4ee59c03" :question/id #uuid "db005b4e-86cd-5194-b2fd-10ca4ee59c03" :question/math-academy-id "q-42021" :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=3 \\\\ -3x-(k+1)y=-9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -(k+1) & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -(k+1) & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -k+5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}1-2y=3 \\\\ -(k-5)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=5,$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+2y=3.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-80130b9b-78a0-54cc-bf84-e036ce6c2ff0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-80130b9b-78a0-54cc-bf84-e036ce6c2ff0" :answer-field/id #uuid "80130b9b-78a0-54cc-bf84-e036ce6c2ff0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cf6dc1f0-4ead-53bf-8e9f-9b57805aa51d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3745dd5b-bc8f-5c5f-bfbb-0a70d0ee8eee" "answer-8c1862b9-030a-5755-b668-e59ca4c9e456" "answer-17602323-8777-51fe-9a70-fac173438e8d" "answer-a1294db0-0da9-5a02-b9e5-791ef34dcf11" "answer-cf6dc1f0-4ead-53bf-8e9f-9b57805aa51d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3745dd5b-bc8f-5c5f-bfbb-0a70d0ee8eee" :answer/id #uuid "3745dd5b-bc8f-5c5f-bfbb-0a70d0ee8eee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c1862b9-030a-5755-b668-e59ca4c9e456" :answer/id #uuid "8c1862b9-030a-5755-b668-e59ca4c9e456" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17602323-8777-51fe-9a70-fac173438e8d" :answer/id #uuid "17602323-8777-51fe-9a70-fac173438e8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1294db0-0da9-5a02-b9e5-791ef34dcf11" :answer/id #uuid "a1294db0-0da9-5a02-b9e5-791ef34dcf11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf6dc1f0-4ead-53bf-8e9f-9b57805aa51d" :answer/id #uuid "cf6dc1f0-4ead-53bf-8e9f-9b57805aa51d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115831 :question/problem "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+3y=1 \\\\  & 6x+(k+3)y=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+3 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 6 & k+3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & k-6 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y=1 \\\\ (k-6)y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=6,$ then the second equation is $0=-8,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186113923 :answer-field/correct "answer-478b28da-a8a3-51e4-963d-8ac53adc010e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-684ddf9d-dd44-5397-b1a8-e6e3ca6a2f95" "answer-545c0eb7-c35a-5d44-b8e2-b045ff203715" "answer-478b28da-a8a3-51e4-963d-8ac53adc010e" "answer-9720657d-4e06-51f7-8e91-da074201b940" "answer-359439f2-81e1-5ced-8482-b2cf08a71409"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-684ddf9d-dd44-5397-b1a8-e6e3ca6a2f95" :answer/id #uuid "684ddf9d-dd44-5397-b1a8-e6e3ca6a2f95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-545c0eb7-c35a-5d44-b8e2-b045ff203715" :answer/id #uuid "545c0eb7-c35a-5d44-b8e2-b045ff203715" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-478b28da-a8a3-51e4-963d-8ac53adc010e" :answer/id #uuid "478b28da-a8a3-51e4-963d-8ac53adc010e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9720657d-4e06-51f7-8e91-da074201b940" :answer/id #uuid "9720657d-4e06-51f7-8e91-da074201b940" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-359439f2-81e1-5ced-8482-b2cf08a71409" :answer/id #uuid "359439f2-81e1-5ced-8482-b2cf08a71409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115832 :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=0 \\\\  & -4x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\n\nII. The system has no solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent independent" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-080f971c-621c-5ccf-b883-b98c49745b79" :activity/id #uuid "080f971c-621c-5ccf-b883-b98c49745b79" :activity/title "Gaussian Elimination For NxM Systems of Equations" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048445 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-2c3254d8-7342-5cba-aa85-c696386c710a" "step-e9dff08f-68e1-5fe8-9586-d7f8edd2598c" "step-3b9e4957-843e-5d56-8704-c60e6e8f032c"] :activity/first-step "step-2c3254d8-7342-5cba-aa85-c696386c710a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c3254d8-7342-5cba-aa85-c696386c710a" :step/id #uuid "2c3254d8-7342-5cba-aa85-c696386c710a" :step/content "question-db005b4e-86cd-5194-b2fd-10ca4ee59c03" :step/next "step-e9dff08f-68e1-5fe8-9586-d7f8edd2598c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e9dff08f-68e1-5fe8-9586-d7f8edd2598c" :step/id #uuid "e9dff08f-68e1-5fe8-9586-d7f8edd2598c" :step/content 17592186115831 :step/next "step-3b9e4957-843e-5d56-8704-c60e6e8f032c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3b9e4957-843e-5d56-8704-c60e6e8f032c" :step/id #uuid "3b9e4957-843e-5d56-8704-c60e6e8f032c" :step/content 17592186115832 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
